\subsection{Ablation studies for \ours{}}
The success of \ours{} relies on the novel design of local-global data distillation, where the selection of regularization loss and the number of iterations for data distillation plays a key role. In this section, we study the choice of regularization loss and its weighting ($\lambda$) in the total loss function. Recall that among the total FL training epochs, we perform local-global distillation on the selected $\tau$ \textit{iterations}, and within each selected \textit{iteration}, the server and clients will perform data updating for some pre-defined \textit{steps}. The effect of local-global distillation \textit{iterations} and data updating \textit{steps} will also be discussed.

